Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Lab 7",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.9363546196688792, 0.47643244068055235`, 0.19354543373769742`]]], "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001768611406839*^9, 4.001768685128284*^9}, {
  4.001768943792872*^9, 4.001768944359778*^9}, {4.001768976994172*^9, 
  4.001768991377529*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"765429c8-dd7e-4b8d-8e0a-\
ad81ebf4b98f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "\n",
 StyleBox["1. How could we use the data from our pendulum simulation to \
compare with the analytical\nsolution? Come up with a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]figure",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9834287022201876, 0.5344930189974822, 0.3070878156710155]],
 StyleBox["-of",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9834287022201876, 0.5344930189974822, 0.3070878156710155]],
 StyleBox["-merit\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \[Dash] some single number \[Dash] \
you can use to quantify\nhow close the simulation and analytical answers are \
for a given angle.",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9834287022201876, 0.5344930189974822, 0.3070878156710155]],
 StyleBox["\n\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["We can use the data from the pendulum simulation to compare the \
plot of the simulated pendulum and the plot given by the analytical solution \
\[Phi][t] = \[Phi]0 Cos[\[Omega]0 t] . To come up with a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]figure-of-merit\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], we can \
integrate from t=0 to t=10 for the difference of the simulation and the \
analytical plots squared: ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "10"], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"x", "[", "t", "]"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"y", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ")"}], "^", "2"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[DifferentialD]", "t"}]}]}]],
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514],ExpressionUUID->
  "4e2c8eeb-fcea-44f9-9c9c-bae99dd6954b"],
 StyleBox[" \n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["\n\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["2. In general, as the initial angle gets higher, what happens to \
the simulation results relative to\nthe analytical results?",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9834287022201876, 0.5344930189974822, 0.3070878156710155]],
 StyleBox["\n\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["In general, as the initial angle gets higher the simulation \
results start to lag behind the analytical results. This is because \
sin(\[Phi]) gets smaller the bigger the angle gets, and the difference \
eventually becomes too big to be able to use small angle approximation.",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["\n\n\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["3. Make a plot of your \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]figure-of-merit\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as a function of angle for at least 5 initial \
pendulum\nangles. Where does the small-angle approximation start to \
significantly deviate from the\nsimulation (let\[CloseCurlyQuote]s say at the \
\[TildeTilde]10% level)?",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9834287022201876, 0.5344930189974822, 0.3070878156710155]],
 StyleBox["\n\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["The small-angle approximation starts to significantly deviate from \
the simulation at around and angle of  40-50 degrees.",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["\n\n\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 StyleBox["4. How would an increase in the mass of the pendulum bob change \
the dynamics (motion) of\nthe system?",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9834287022201876, 0.5344930189974822, 0.3070878156710155]],
 StyleBox["\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 "\n",
 StyleBox["An increase in the mass of the pendulum would not change the \
dynamics of the system. The mass is not in the final equation of motion for a \
pendulum and so would have no effect on the system.\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[
   0.9637903410391394, 0.8222476539253833, 0.6639658197909514]],
 "\n"
}], "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.001768705538322*^9, 4.001768711839057*^9}, {
   4.0017687769343357`*^9, 4.001768784820875*^9}, {4.0017688194198437`*^9, 
   4.001768879403805*^9}, {4.0017690090450897`*^9, 4.001769066876424*^9}, {
